window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["0f"]={"https://theconversation.com/a-melbourne-cup-runner-in-a-skip-bin-is-shocking-but-a-lot-of-dead-horses-end-up-at-the-tip-296828":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"96a81aee55053fb75990e98f1f7cfc010bb9b12f4f50c7a3cc89c3019b6f80fc","read":"https://theconversation.com/a-melbourne-cup-runner-in-a-skip-bin-is-shocking-but-a-lot-of-dead-horses-end-up-at-the-tip-296828","bytes":178049,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"A Melbourne Cup runner in a skip bin is shocking – but a lot of dead horses end up at the tip","by":[{"n":"Cathrynne Henshall","r":"Post-doctoral Fellow, School of Agricultural, Environmental and Veterinary Sciences, Charles Sturt University"}],"pub":"2026-11-17T08:41:53Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["This article contains details of animal deaths some readers may find distressing."]},{"k":"p","s":["Late on Tuesday afternoon, the body of ",["Melbourne Cup racehorse","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-03/melbourne-cup-2026-finishing-order-from-first-to-last/107340766"]," So You Are was ",["found in a skip bin","https://www.theage.com.au/sport/racing/melbourne-cup-runner-suspected-to-be-horse-found-in-sydney-skip-bin-20261117-p61ex8.html"]," at a rubbish tip in Sydney."]},{"k":"p","s":["The five-year-old gelding had been rushed to an equine specialist with severe colic (a gastro-intestinal illness) and was euthanised when the issue could not be resolved. A builder at the tip filmed the body and posted the video."]},{"k":"p","s":["The vet hospital said its contracted provider took the horse to the landfill where he should have been buried promptly. It has apologised."]},{"k":"p","s":["Racing NSW, which is ",["conducting an investigation","https://thestraight.com.au/lucas-heights-horse-carcass-investigation/"],", stated So You Are was ",["awaiting burial","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-11-17/dead-melbourne-cup-runner-so-you-are-found-in-sydney-skip-bin/107395274"]," when the video was recorded."]},{"k":"h","s":["What normally happens when horses die or are euthanised?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many horse owners cannot bury a dead horse at home – they may not own a property or may lack the space or distance from water bodies to safely bury a horse."]},{"k":"p","s":["An adult horse weighs around 500 kilograms, and a burial pit needs ",["at least two metres of soil","https://www.dpird.nsw.gov.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0011/1624196/PRIMEFACT-Emergency-Animal-Disease-EAD-Animal-carcass-disposal-04-2026.pdf"]," over the carcass."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is common practice for vets to dispose of dead horses at licensed landfills. The standard procedure is carcasses are placed in designated areas and covered without delay. NSW Department of Primary Industries ",["guidance lists","https://www.dpird.nsw.gov.au/__data/assets/pdf_file/0011/1624196/PRIMEFACT-Emergency-Animal-Disease-EAD-Animal-carcass-disposal-04-2026.pdf"]," licensed landfill as the preferred disposal option in most instances."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some horses killed by ",["captive bolt tools","https://vetmed.iastate.edu/vdpam/about/focus-areas/animal-welfare/animal-welfare-focus/euthanasia-anatomical-landmarks/gunshot-or-penetrating-captive-bolt/"]," (where compressed gas or a specialised cartridge delivers high-velocity impacts) or firearms ",["may be accepted by knackeries","https://kb.rspca.org.au/categories/farmed-animals/slaughter-killing/how-is-animal-welfare-regulated-at-australian-knackeries"]," for rendering or use in pet food."]},{"k":"p","s":["However this option is not available if drugs have been used to euthanise the horse."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why the euthanasia drugs matter"]},{"k":"p","s":["Vets usually euthanise horses with ",["an overdose of a barbiturate","https://aaep.org/resource/euthanasia-guidelines/"],", given intravenously."]},{"k":"p","s":["The drug will depress breathing, brain activity and ultimately the heart. During the euthanasia process it will be carried by the blood stream throughout the body, leading to high concentrations in organs such as the kidneys, lungs and liver."]},{"k":"p","s":["Because it is slow to break down, it will remain in tissue long after death. This can poison animals which consume the carcass."]},{"k":"p","s":["In one reported case, ",["dogs were poisoned","https://doi.org/10.1177/104063871002200423"]," after scavenging a partly buried horse that had been euthanised two years earlier."]},{"k":"p","s":["Studies of composted horse carcasses have found the drug still present in compost and liquids leaching from the soil."]},{"k":"p","s":["Any animal that eats the tissue can be sedated, anaesthetised or killed. A review of reported cases found most poisoned wild animals were scavenging birds, and 86% of those were eagles or their relatives."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dogs are the most often ",["reported domestic victims","https://doi.org/10.1055/a-2768-0972"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why a skip bin is a problem"]},{"k":"p","s":["Prompt and deep burial removes this risk. A carcass in an open skip, even for a short time, is within reach of birds and may be moved on with general waste rather than deeply buried."]},{"k":"p","s":["If left in the bin for an extended period, the decomposition process can lead to unpleasant odours and carcasses can be a breeding ground for flies which can transmit disease."]},{"k":"p","s":["How So You Are came to be in the bin instead of buried, and for how long, is for the investigation to establish."]},{"k":"p","s":["The risks of secondary poisoning are well understood by the veterinary profession which is why vet practices establish relationships with local landfills."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why a horse in a skip bin shocks us"]},{"k":"p","s":["Much of the reaction to the video has nothing to do with how So You Are was euthanised under veterinary care."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many are reacting to the sight of a specific horse, a Melbourne Cup runner with a brand on his shoulder, lying among building waste as if he were household rubbish."]},{"k":"p","s":["Such treatment seems a callous contradiction to industry narratives of how much care horses receive and how well they are loved."]},{"k":"p","s":["It contravenes our expectations of how the body of a deceased equine “athlete” should be treated. The reverent burial of champions ",["such as Makybe Diva","https://www.abc.net.au/news/2026-02-28/horse-racing-makybe-diva-dad-after-health-battle/106400516"]," appear to honour the service given by horses to racing."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["How are racehorses really treated in the ‘sport of kings’?","https://theconversation.com/how-are-racehorses-really-treated-in-the-sport-of-kings-240998"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Tuesday’s video makes visible something that is usually hidden. Even after the best veterinary care, dead horses end up in local tips."]},{"k":"p","s":["Landfill burial may appear more respectful than a skip bin, but its purpose is sanitary and to protect wildlife: it is still burial in a rubbish dump."]},{"k":"h","s":["A dead horse has no welfare"]},{"k":"p","s":["For So You Are, the dumping of his body in the bin is not an animal welfare issue. Welfare concerns what an animal experiences: pain, fear, comfort, pleasure. A dead horse experiences nothing and has no interest in what happens to its body."]},{"k":"p","s":["The distress belongs to the people who cared for him, and the real risk is to the animals that might eat from the carcass."]},{"k":"p","s":["For the horse, what mattered was how he lived and how he died."]},{"k":"p","s":["By the hospital’s account, he received emergency care and was euthanised under anaesthesia, about as good an end as a horse with fatal colic can have."]},{"k":"p","s":["If this case makes us care more about horses, that attention belongs with the living: how they are housed, trained, raced and retired, and whether their deaths are timely and humane."]}],"chars":4996},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"3b262f16a51b1a1b5c4359c836038bf1a95af22e775d8f588dfc7738b4bc97a2","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/israel","bytes":124368,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Israel travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-08T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-10-27T16:05:38+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Gaza"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Gaza"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Areas near Gaza"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel within 500m of the border with Gaza"]},{"k":"hs","s":["The West Bank"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tulkarm Governorate, Jenin Governorate, and Tubas Governorate except Route 90"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Northern Israel and Occupied Golan Heights"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Areas north of Route 89 between Nahariyya and Dalton; north of a straight eastward line from Dalton to Route 91; and north of Route 91 across the Golan Heights, excluding routes 89 and 91 themselves"]},{"k":"li","s":["Within 500m of the Area of Separation in the occupied Golan Heights (the ‘Alpha line’). Do not attempt to enter the occupied Golan Heights through Syria"]},{"k":"li","s":["Sheba’a Farms and Ghajja"]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against all but essential travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["West Bank"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["The rest of the West Bank, except for: East Jerusalem, Bethlehem Governate, Ramallah Municipality, Jericho municipality and all areas which lie south of it (this includes the Allenby crossing). Highway 1 that links Jerusalem and Tel Aviv and the areas that lie to the south and west of the Highway (this includes Highway 3), and Route 443 and Highway 45 which link Jerusalem and Tel Aviv"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional tensions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The context in the Middle East remains deeply unpredictable and the risk of sudden escalation is high. Since conflict began in early 2026, Iran has stated its intention to target locations associated with the US and Israel, including, but not limited to, organisations, businesses, facilities, and institutions. There have been strikes and retaliatory attacks by Iran and others across the region against civilian and US military infrastructure."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals in, or planning to travel through, the Middle East should be prepared for possible flight cancellations, airspace closures, and travel disruptions. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["read ",["If you’re affected by a crisis abroad - GOV.UK","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],". This includes guidance on “how to prepare for a crisis” with suggestions on what you might include in your emergency supplies and “what to do in a crisis”"]},{"k":"li","s":["sign up to ",["FCDO Travel Advice email alerts","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/email-signup"]]},{"k":"li","s":["follow advice from the local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local and international media for the latest information, including updates relating to airports and airspace which could close at short notice"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay away from areas around security or military facilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["keep your departure plans under review, and ensure your travel documents are up to date"]},{"k":"li","s":["if advised to take shelter, stay indoors or find the nearest safe building or designated shelter. An interior stairwell or a room with as few external walls or windows as possible may provide additional protection. The greatest risk is from falling debris caused by intercepts, and you are safest inside a secure structure. Do not approach or touch any drone or missile fragments or unusual objects"]},{"k":"h","s":["Shelter in place"]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow the instructions of the local authorities. If you are advised to take shelter, ",["Israel’s Home Front Command provides guidance on how to find a protected space","https://www.oref.org.il/eng/emergencies/protection-guidelines"],". The best option is a residential protected space (Mamad, Mamak or Maman) or a communal shelter. If that is not possible, choose a stairwell without windows and exterior walls and stay at its centre."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to receive information and alerts. Visit ",["Israel’s Home Front Command","https://www.oref.org.il/eng"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["If you are in Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to ongoing regional tensions, we recommend against all travel to some parts of Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["The situation could escalate quickly and poses significant risks. Regional tensions may cause international borders (air and land) to close."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in Israel and Palestine, be aware that whilst the frequency of missile and drone attacks has decreased there is a risk of rocket and drone attacks throughout Israel. There is a risk of shrapnel from intercepted missiles falling across Israel and Palestine, and possible disruption at Ben Gurion airport in Tel Aviv."]},{"k":"p","s":["Political tension can cause demonstrations and clashes around anniversaries and significant events."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep up to date through local media and follow the instructions of Israeli Home Front Command. To find these:"]},{"k":"li","s":["visit the Israeli Home Front Command website (available in Israel only)."]},{"k":"li","s":["call 104 if you are in Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before travelling within Israel or Palestine, check the local measures in place, that roads are open and, where appropriate, that scheduled train and bus services are operating."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travel within or out of Israel or Palestine is at your own risk. You are encouraged to follow the advice of local authorities, for example on which routes are open or when to take shelter."]},{"k":"h","s":["Leaving Gaza"]},{"k":"p","s":["Border crossings out of Gaza have been closed to civilians and general traffic since the Israeli military took control of the Rafah crossing on 6 May 2024. Consular support is not available from within Gaza. If you are a British national in Gaza who wants to leave Gaza, you should make contact with us as soon as possible. There are currently no exit routes available for foreign nationals to depart Gaza independently. We are working with the Israeli, Palestinian and other authorities in the region to help British nationals leave via safe routes."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a UK visa holder who meets all of the following criteria, you can contact us to request support to leave Gaza if:"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have a spouse/partner or a child aged 17 or under currently living in the UK, and"]},{"k":"li","s":["you hold valid permission to enter or remain in the UK for longer than 6 months"]},{"k":"h","s":["Help from other organisations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep up to date with local travel advice through local news outlets and international outlets like the Access Coordination Unit."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide and any specific travel advice that applies to you:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["disabled travellers","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["volunteering and adventure travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help British nationals make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice covers Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK who choose to travel despite FCDO advice. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Israel and Palestine set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Israeli Embassy in London","https://embassies.gov.il/london/Pages/default.aspx"]," or the ",["Palestinian Mission to the UK","https://palmissionuk.org/consular-affairs-ar/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check Israeli immigration policies before you travel. Allow extra time for increased security measures and checks at airports, especially during Israeli holidays and during the summer tourist season."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Israel or Palestine, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 90 days after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Israel without a visa as a tourist. On entry, visitors get permission to stay for up to 3 months. However, if you are a dual national, read the ",["dual nationals guidance","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/entry-requirements#british-people-holding-dual-nationality"]," for more information."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you work in Israel without the proper permissions, you can be detained and deported. This process could take several months."]},{"k":"h","s":["Electronic Travel Authorisation (ETA)"]},{"k":"p","s":["As of 1 January 2025, to visit Israel you will need to get an Electronic Travel Authorisation (ETA) before you arrive. The ETA is valid for 2 years and covers a visit of 90 days. It will cost 25 new Israeli shekels. You can check your eligibility and ",["apply for an ETA with the Israel Population and Immigration authority","https://israel-entry.piba.gov.il/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Passport stamping and entry cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Visitors entering via Tel Aviv Ben Gurion Airport get an entry card instead of an entry stamp in their passport. At other entry points to the country, you may get an entry card or you may get a stamp."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep your entry card with your passport until you leave. This is evidence that you entered Israel legally. You may need it, particularly if you’re crossing into Palestine. If you’re refused entry to Israel, your passport may be stamped with an entry stamp and 2 red lines drawn across it to show the refusal."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Stamps with restrictions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Entry stamps that state ‘Palestinian Authority only’ or ‘Judea and Samaria only’ have been issued to some travellers at:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Allenby Bridge crossing with Jordan"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tel Aviv Ben Gurion Airport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Since travellers entering by the Allenby Bridge crossing must pass through Israeli checkpoints and Israeli-controlled territory to reach Jerusalem or Gaza, this effectively limits travellers who receive this stamp."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is not clear how travellers who get this stamp at Tel Aviv Ben Gurion Airport can leave the airport without violating the restriction."]},{"k":"p","s":["This stamp has been issued to travellers who have no Palestinian or other Arab ancestry, and do not seem to have a claim to a Palestinian Authority ID."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Immigration checks"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Israeli authorities decide if you can enter Israel. You may experience lengthy personal questioning and baggage searches at security when you enter and leave Israel. Some visitors may face longer searches and questioning, including those:"]},{"k":"li","s":["with Palestinian or Arab ancestry, or with ancestry of a country that is predominantly Muslim"]},{"k":"li","s":["with evidence of previous travel which may be considered suspicious"]},{"k":"li","s":["who are considered to have publicly criticised the state of Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals can legally be refused entry if they:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have publicly called for a boycott of Israel or Israeli settlements"]},{"k":"li","s":["belong to an organisation which has called for a boycott"]},{"k":"li","s":["have publicly made statements denying the Holocaust or the October 7 terrorist attack"]},{"k":"li","s":["have publicly made statements of support for the prosecution of Israeli citizens in a foreign country or in an international court for actions they took during their military duties for Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers, particularly those who fall into these categories, may be held at border control for more checks, sometimes for several hours, including in detention facilities. Israeli security has sometimes requested access to travellers’ personal email or social media accounts as a condition of entry. Your baggage or digital devices may also be searched and could be withheld."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Previous travel to countries in the region"]},{"k":"p","s":["Evidence of previous travel to another country in the region, such as entry or exit stamps in your passport, does not normally stop you entering Israel. However, you may face extra questioning at the border."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have concerns about visas or entry into Israel, including whether previous travel can affect you travelling there, contact the Israeli Embassy in the UK before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refusal of entry into Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re refused entry to Israel, you will be booked on the next available flight back to where you flew in from, on the same airline."]},{"k":"p","s":["Depending on the flight schedule, you may be taken to the Immigration Detention Centre (a few minutes’ drive from the airport) to wait until your flight departs. You will have access to a telephone, information in English and medical assistance if needed. Your luggage will stay at the airport, so tell officials if you need to retrieve anything urgent from your luggage, for example medication."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can contact the ",["British Embassy in Israel","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-embassy-tel-aviv"]," from the detention centre. They can help where possible but cannot intervene in immigration decisions."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entering Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Israeli authorities control entry to Palestine, including by sea to Gaza. You must show a passport and Israeli immigration slip to cross between Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read about the ",["requirements for foreign nationals entering the West Bank on the Israeli government website","https://www.gov.il/en/departments/policies/judeaentry2022"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Israeli border officials at Tel Aviv Ben Gurion Airport have asked some travellers to sign a form stating they are not allowed to enter territories controlled by the Palestinian Authority unless they get advance authorisation from the Israeli ‘Territory Actions Co-ordinator’. You can be deported from Israel and barred from entry for up to 10 years for violating this restriction."]},{"k":"p","s":["If immigration officials believe you plan to enter Gaza without permission, or that you’re entering Israel to work in Palestine, they may refuse you entry."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO cannot support your application for entry or exit permits for Gaza. If you decide to visit Gaza against FCDO advice, you must contact the relevant authorities well in advance. FCDO cannot provide administrative support to UK charities wishing to enter Gaza by the Rafah crossing."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Rafah border regularly closes with no warning and for long periods. The Erez border is currently closed. At these times it may be impossible to enter or leave Gaza."]},{"k":"p","s":["Israeli checkpoints may close on Israeli public holidays and during periods of increased instability. There have been increased movement and access restrictions across the West Bank with unpredictable opening and closing times. There is information on ",["known checkpoint closures on the UN website","https://www.accesscoordination.org/"],". This can change at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign nationals may encounter suspicion or hostility at checkpoints and in areas not frequented by foreign nationals."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["British nationals of Palestinian origin"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a British national of Palestinian origin (on the Palestinian Population Register or holding a Palestinian ID number), you must have a Palestinian passport or travel document to leave Gaza or the West Bank."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a British national with a Palestinian name or place of birth but without a Palestinian ID number, you may face problems. British nationals of Palestinian origin or British nationals married to Palestinians have been refused entry into Israel."]},{"k":"h","s":["British people holding dual nationality"]},{"k":"p","s":["British-Palestinian dual nationals living in the West Bank and Gaza may only exit Palestine through the Allenby border crossing into Jordan or the Rafah border crossing into Egypt. They must return by the same route."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re a British-Palestinian dual national entering Gaza against FCDO travel advice, check entry and exit procedures with the relevant authorities. There is a limit on the number of dual nationals permitted to enter and exit Gaza through Erez – this includes if you are entering for medical or humanitarian reasons. The Israeli government has the authority to make decisions on entry and exit permits through Erez."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your nearest Israeli embassy if you need pre-approval to travel to Israel. Dual nationals holding Iranian, Iraqi, Syrian and Lebanese citizenship have previously been affected. If you are not a citizen of any of these countries, but have close family ties, you should check with your nearest Israeli embassy before travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["Children with at least one Israeli parent (father or mother) are considered Israeli nationals. These children must enter and leave Israel on an Israeli passport."]},{"k":"h","s":["British nationals with associations with other countries in the region"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dual nationals holding Iranian, Iraqi, Syrian and Lebanese citizenship have previously been heavily questioned, denied entry and deported. If a deportation flight is not available immediately, this can mean being detained until one is available, which can take a number of days. If you are a citizen of any of these countries, or have associations such as close family ties, the Israeli authorities advise you to check with your nearest Israeli embassy before travel to get pre-approval for entry."]},{"k":"h","s":["Children and young people"]},{"k":"p","s":["Children aged 17 and under travelling to Israel alone or with only one parent should carry a letter from their parents or guardians confirming parental consent, accommodation plans and contact details."]},{"k":"p","s":["Children exiting Israel alone should carry a locally-issued notarised letter as advised by ",["external law firms","https://lawoffice.org.il/en/unaccompanied-minors-traveling-abroad-from-israel/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For children with at least one Israeli parent, read the advice for dual nationals above."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry to Egypt"]},{"k":"p","s":["Egypt-Israel border crossing (opening times are subject to change):"]},{"k":"li","s":["Taba: Open 24 hours"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to cross the border from Israel into Egypt at Taba, we recommend you bring at least 170 US dollars (cash) per person, with some extra US dollars in cash to cover any further expenses. Since early March 2026, border crossing charges at Taba have been subject to increases at short notice."]},{"k":"li","s":["If staying in Taba, travellers will need to pay a border tax of 20 US dollars. The border tax allows you to obtain an entry permission stamp for a stay of up to 15 days"]},{"k":"li","s":["If travelling further than Taba, including to Sharm El-Sheikh, but remaining within the Sinai Peninsula, travellers will need to pay a border tax of 120 US dollars. The border tax allows you to obtain an entry permission stamp for a stay of up to 15 days"]},{"k":"li","s":["If travelling beyond the Sinai Peninsula, including to fly from airports such as Cairo and Hurghada, travellers will need to pay a border tax of 120 US dollars and purchase a standard entry visa for 30 US dollars. At Taba, this entry visa also requires a “letter of guarantee”, provided by travel agents and costing around 20 USD. Both the visa and the “letter of guarantee” can be purchased at the Border Crossing"]},{"k":"p","s":["If travelling by car through the Taba Border Crossing you may also be required to pay 100 US dollars and additional amounts for parking."]},{"k":"p","s":["Please note that ATMs at the Taba Border Crossing are unreliable and frequently run out of cash. Travellers should obtain USD before travelling or in Eilat before arriving at the Crossing as all payments are required in cash."]},{"k":"p","s":["Border officials may ask travellers to remove hats, coats or other items of clothing, including religious clothing, as they pass through the Taba Border Crossing terminal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry to Jordan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Land crossings to Jordan may be restricted or close at short notice, including due to trade union strikes. More information is available on the ",["Israel Airport Authority website","https://www.iaa.gov.il/en/land-border-crossings/alenbi/notifications-and-updates/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Jordan-Israel border crossings (opening times are subject to change):"]},{"k":"li","s":["Allenby/King Hussein Bridge"]},{"k":"li","s":["The Northern (Jordan River/Sheikh Hussein) crossing"]},{"k":"li","s":["The Southern (Yitzhak Rabin/Wadi Araba) crossing"]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip, check the vaccinations and certificates you need in ",["TravelHealthPro’s Israel guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/110/israel#Vaccine_Recommendations"]," and ",["TravelHealthPro’s Palestinian guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/173/palestinian#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Israel and Palestine","https://www.gov.il/en/departments/topics/customs_israel_tax_authority/govil-landing-page"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Israeli Tax Authority provides information on ",["taking money into or out of Israel","https://www.gov.il/en/departments/guides/guide-requirement-report-and-spend-money-on-israel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice covers Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"h","s":["Conflict between Lebanese Hizballah and Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Following the conflict between Israel and Lebanese Hizballah (LH), a cessation of hostilities was announced on 16 April 2026. However, fighting continues and the dynamic nature of the conflict means the situation may change quickly."]},{"k":"p","s":["There remains a risk that hostilities could reignite, and with little warning. Check Home Front Command for the latest guidance. Restrictions may be put in place at short notice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Conflict between Iran and Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Following the conflict between Israel and Iran a ceasefire was agreed on 8 April 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["There remains a risk that hostilities could reignite, and with little warning. Check Home Front Command for the latest guidance. Restrictions may be put in place at short notice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Conflict between the Houthis (in Yemen) and Israel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Following the conflict between Israel and the Houthis (in Yemen), there continues to be a risk of missile and drone attacks throughout Israel. There is a risk of shrapnel from intercepted missiles falling across Israel and Palestine and possible disruption at Ben Gurion airport. On 22 and 24 September 2025, two drones fired by the Houthis fell in Eilat, injuring at least 20 people."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check Home Front Command for the latest guidance. Restrictions may be put in place at short notice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Conflict in Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["On 7 October 2023 there was a large-scale terrorist attack by Hamas in southern Israel. The frequency of attacks has significantly decreased but there is still a risk of rocket attacks throughout Israel."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is an increased risk of political tension which can cause demonstrations and clashes around anniversaries and significant events."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["There was a large-scale terrorist attack by Hamas into southern Israel on 7 October 2023 where over 1,200 people were killed. Hamas continue to launch rockets into Israel and the Israeli Defence Forces are conducting significant military activity in Gaza."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Israel and Palestine are very likely to continue with an increased threat of attacks, including by individuals acting alone."]},{"k":"p","s":["Any attacks could be indiscriminate, including places visited by foreign nationals such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Old City in Jerusalem"]},{"k":"li","s":["government, military and police installations"]},{"k":"li","s":["security personnel including military and police"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport networks"]},{"k":"li","s":["businesses with western interests"]},{"k":"li","s":["crowded places"]},{"k":"p","s":["Areas where foreign nationals and tourists are known to gather may be at higher risk of attack. Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Examples of recent significant attacks include:"]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2025:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in September, six people were killed and eight wounded in a shooting attack in northern Jerusalem"]},{"k":"li","s":["in March, one person was killed and one person injured in a shooting attack in northern Israel"]},{"k":"li","s":["in March, one person was killed and 3 injured in a stabbing attack in Haifa"]},{"k":"li","s":["in February, one person was killed and 12 people were injured in a ramming and stabbing attack at Karkur Junction near Pardes Hana-Karkur, south of Haifa"]},{"k":"li","s":["in February, 3 bombs exploded on 3 separate busses in the Tel Aviv area. Two other buses were found with bombs which failed to explode. There were no casualties. See our Regional Risks section for further information on using public transport in Tel Aviv"]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2024:"]},{"k":"li","s":["7 people were killed in a shooting and stabbing attack in Jaffa"]},{"k":"li","s":["3 people were killed in a shooting attack at the Allenby Bridge Crossing"]},{"k":"li","s":["one person was killed and 17 injured during a ramming attack in Ra’anana"]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2023:"]},{"k":"li","s":["3 people were killed during a shooting attack in the Jordan Valley"]},{"k":"li","s":["one person was killed and 6 people injured during a car-ramming incident in Tel Aviv"]},{"k":"li","s":["one person was killed and 3 people injured in a shooting attack in Tel Aviv"]},{"k":"li","s":["7 people were killed and 3 injured during a shooting attack in Neve Yaakov, East Jerusalem"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorist kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist kidnap is a risk in Gaza and along the border with Egypt. On 7 October 2023, 251 people were kidnapped by Hamas into Gaza."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government is to not make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["There was an ongoing conflict between Israel and Hamas following the October 7 2023 Hamas terrorist attack which saw 251 people kidnapped into Gaza. On 10 October, Hamas and Israel agreed to a ceasefire."]},{"k":"p","s":["There remains a risk that hostilities could reignite, and with little warning. You should check Home Front Command for the latest guidance. Restrictions may be put in place at short notice. If travelling near military operation areas, follow all Israeli official instructions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Military activity continues on the Gaza border. Keep up to date with the news while travelling."]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep up to date with local travel advice on local news outlets and international outlets like the Access Coordination Unit."]},{"k":"p","s":["Rocket fire can affect most areas of Israel and the interception of missiles over Palestine may result in falling fragments or debris. Israeli air strikes also continue into Gaza. Be cautious and make sure you know the safety actions that you should take if an Israeli warning siren sounds. Follow ",["advice from local authorities","https://www.idf.il/en/minisites/regional-commands/home-front-command/how-to-act-during-an-alert/"]," and stay informed of the security situation through the media and this travel advice. No warning sirens will sound inside Gaza, or in the West Bank outside of Israeli settlements. See ",["Regional risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/regional-risks#gaza"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent incidents"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Israel and the West Bank, there is a risk of violent incidents, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["stabbings"]},{"k":"li","s":["shootings"]},{"k":"li","s":["arson"]},{"k":"li","s":["vehicle rammings"]},{"k":"li","s":["stone throwing attacks on people and vehicles"]},{"k":"li","s":["explosions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Incidents have occurred:"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Tel Aviv"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Be’er Sheva"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Hadera"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Jerusalem and the Old City, particularly at and around: Damascus Gate"]},{"k":"li","s":["Herod’s gate"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lion’s Gate"]},{"k":"li","s":["Chain Gate"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Nablus"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Jenin"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Hebron"]},{"k":"li","s":["in Jordan Valley"]},{"k":"li","s":["along Route 60 (especially junctions near Nablus), Route 443 and other West Bank arterial roads used by both Palestinians and Israelis"]},{"k":"li","s":["at Israeli checkpoints"]},{"k":"p","s":["Incidents have involved protestors (Israelis and Palestinians), Israeli security forces and civilians (including Israeli settlers). Tourists or bystanders could be caught up in incidents."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Demonstrations and armed clashes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Large political demonstrations can:"]},{"k":"li","s":["happen across Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"li","s":["happen at short notice and often turn violent"]},{"k":"li","s":["affect entry and exit to Ben Gurion Airport in Tel Aviv – check before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check local news before travelling for information on recent clashes"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid large gatherings and demonstrations"]},{"k":"li","s":["check locally before travelling to areas where there has been recent violence and follow the instructions of the local authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["If Israeli security operations or armed clashes are happening near you, stay inside and wait for the local authorities to confirm that the situation is calm before moving to a different location."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is increased risk of political tension, which can cause demonstrations and clashes, during events such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Thursday and Saturday evenings"]},{"k":"li","s":["after Friday prayers"]},{"k":"li","s":["Jewish high holidays (Passover, Rosh Hashana, Yom Kippur and Succoth)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Ramadan, in particular Laylat Al Qadr"]},{"k":"li","s":["other religious holidays"]},{"k":"li","s":["anniversaries including 7 October, Independence Day (14 May, Hebrew calendar dates vary), Jerusalem Day (date varies), Land Day (30 March), Nakba Day (15 May)"]},{"k":"p","s":["Risks increase when religious or national holidays overlap."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some of these protests have led to violent clashes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refugee camps"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be extremely cautious if visiting refugee camps. Hebron and Palestinian refugee camps have previously been the site of violent clashes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Settlements"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been recent violent incidents in settlements and settlement outposts, including near Beit El, Homesh, Shilo and Evyatar."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep your personal belongings in a safe place. Theft of passports, credit cards, and valuables from public beaches is common."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry ID, for example, a copy of the personal details and entry stamp pages of your passport)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Dress code"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Jerusalem, the West Bank and Gaza, clothing should cover your shoulders, upper arms, and legs above the knee."]},{"k":"p","s":["Locals in ultra-Orthodox Jewish neighbourhoods such as Bnei Brak, Modi’in Illit, Beitar Illit, Beit Shemesh and Safed can react strongly to anyone, particularly women, dressed less conservatively. Check locations of ultra-Orthodox neighbourhoods and towns in travel guides."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country. If you are in Palestine during this time, do not:"]},{"k":"li","s":["eat, drink, smoke or chew gum in public in the daytime, including in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["play loud music or dance"]},{"k":"li","s":["swear in public"]},{"k":"p","s":["Children aged 7 and under do not fast during Ramadan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Access and prayers at Al-Aqsa Mosque during Ramadan have seen restrictions and heightened security measures by Israeli authorities. This includes age and gender-based entry restrictions, and routine physical searches. There will be a heightened security environment and tense atmosphere during Ramadan in the Old City."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that if hotels and restaurants are providing food or drink in fasting hours, they may separate you from Islamic guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that driving may be erratic, particularly when people are trying to get home at dusk or be aware that fasting can cause tiredness, particularly during the later afternoon and early evening"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Buying property"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are risks in buying property in Israeli settlements on land considered to be occupied under international law in East Jerusalem, the rest of the West Bank and the Golan. A future peace deal between Israel and the Palestinians, or between Israel and Syria, could have consequences for property you buy in these settlements."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO does not offer legal advice on or become involved in private property disputes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re caught with drugs, you can expect a prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be sensitive about taking pictures of people in Muslim and Orthodox Jewish areas. Do not take photographs of military or police officers or installations."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Israeli law does not criminalise same-sex sexual relations between consenting adults. In Palestine, same-sex sexual activity is legal in the West Bank but illegal in Gaza, where it carries a 10-year prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attitudes towards LGBT+ issues in some parts of Palestinian and Israeli society can be hostile."]},{"k":"p","s":["In more conservative Israeli areas in the West Bank, including in ultra-Orthodox communities, if you show affection in public, regardless of your gender or sexuality, you may receive negative attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["In Palestinian society, same-sex relationships are largely taboo. Some Palestinian groups may violently oppose cultural events and demonstrations, which they see as inconsistent with their values. This includes those seen as linked to the LGBT+ community, even if the event is not intended to promote LGBT+ rights. In these cases, the Palestinian security forces and police may not always act effectively to protect participants. Be aware of these risks. Liaise with local authorities before planning or organising any event."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tel Aviv has a large, active LGBT+ community and a big annual Pride parade. Jerusalem also has an annual Pride parade, but there has been a heavy security presence at the event since a fatal stabbing in 2015. Be aware of your personal security if attending."]},{"k":"p","s":["See more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re caught breaking local laws on import and export of wild animals, expect to receive a substantial fine and up to 2 years in prison. For more information on the regulations and laws in Israel see the ",["Israeli Nature and Park Authority website","https://en.parks.org.il/%D7%99%D7%91%D7%95%D7%90-%D7%95%D7%99%D7%A6%D7%95%D7%90-%D7%97%D7%99%D7%95%D7%AA-%D7%91%D7%A8-%D7%95%D7%A2%D7%A8%D7%9B%D7%99-%D7%98%D7%91%D7%A2-%D7%9E%D7%95%D7%92%D7%A0%D7%99%D7%9D/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Israel and Palestine, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must ",["carry a green card","https://www.gov.uk/vehicle-insurance/driving-abroad"]," to prove you have the minimum insurance cover."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent road accidents due to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["erratic driving"]},{"k":"li","s":["unreliable vehicle maintenance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police operate radar speed traps on some roads and issue heavy fines for speeding."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid driving into ultra-Orthodox Jewish areas of Jerusalem on Shabbat. Shabbat is from sunset on Friday to nightfall on Saturday. If you attempt to drive into these areas, local residents may throw stones at your car."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiring a car"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to drive across into the West Bank, check your insurance will cover you there. Some hire companies do not insure vehicles taken there. It may be easier to hire a fully insured car from a company in East Jerusalem."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hitchhiking"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is not safe to hitchhike in Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving in the desert"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re travelling to the desert, you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["go with others"]},{"k":"li","s":["take a supply of water"]},{"k":"li","s":["take a mobile phone"]},{"k":"li","s":["let someone know your itinerary and expected return time"]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Roads can flood during extreme weather conditions. Flash flooding is a risk, particularly in the arid southern region of the Negev. Check risk areas locally."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes are a risk in Israel and Palestine. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice covers Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Israel and Palestine. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Jerusalem"]},{"k":"p","s":["Since 7 October Israeli authorities have limited access to Jerusalem, and Israel in general, for residents of the West Bank, enforcing age and gender-specific restrictions for entry, particularly during Ramadan. While women aged 51 or over and men aged 56 or over with special permits have been granted entry for prayers, many potential worshippers have been turned away. Additionally, there have been routine instances of physical searches and detentions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Street protests and demonstrations can happen across Jerusalem, including East Jerusalem and the Old City. Check local news ahead of travel and follow instructions of local authorities. Avoid demonstrations and large gatherings."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent demonstrations in many of the areas visited by tourists in the Old City and after Friday prayers. Areas include in and around:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Damascus Gate"]},{"k":"li","s":["Herod’s Gate"]},{"k":"li","s":["Lion’s Gate"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Chain Gate"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some protests have led to violent clashes. Be aware of your surroundings at all times and leave the area if there is evidence of tension or unrest, for example if the shops in the souks of the Old City suddenly begin to close their shutters. The entrances to the Old City may have additional checks, or may close."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been a number of violent incidents on public transport and near public transport lines. Take extra care when using public transport in Jerusalem."]},{"k":"h","s":["Tel Aviv"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take extra care when using public transport in Tel Aviv, in particular at transport hubs, and when using buses in the greater Tel Aviv area. Consider using other forms of transport."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been large political demonstrations in Tel Aviv. Entry and exit to Ben Gurion airport has occasionally been impacted during demonstrations."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas near Gaza"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been repeated instances of rocket fire from Gaza, which may reach well beyond the Gaza border area. Israel has often responded with air strikes into Gaza. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure you know the safety actions to take if an Israeli warning siren sounds – no warning sirens will sound inside Gaza"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow ",["advice from local authorities","https://www.idf.il/en/minisites/regional-commands/home-front-command/how-to-act-during-an-alert/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["stay informed of the security situation through the media"]},{"k":"h","s":["Gaza"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Gaza (including the waters off Gaza)."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should not approach the perimeter fence surrounding the Gaza Strip."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO cannot offer routine consular assistance in Gaza. If you travel to Gaza against our advice, review your security arrangements regularly."]},{"k":"p","s":["The border crossings with Israel (Erez) and Egypt (Rafah) may close with no notice. Check the status of the Rafah crossing into Egypt before you travel. Movement to the Rafah crossing and beyond is at your own risk. Currently, the Rafah border regularly closes with no warning and for long periods. The Erez border has been closed since October 2023."]},{"k":"p","s":["There will be no warning siren inside Gaza and there are no official air raid shelters. Take advice from locals about the safest place to shelter."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO cannot help individuals applying for entry or exit permits for Gaza. See ",["entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/entry-requirements"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO recognises that major international organisations need to carry out humanitarian and reconstruction work and engage in independent reporting and verification of the situation in Gaza. Medical and other essential specialist staff should co-ordinate their entry to and exit from Gaza with those organisations."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not enter Gaza by sea, including via a flotilla delivering humanitarian aid. The Israeli Navy routinely patrols the area and will prevent any vessels attempting to breach the restrictions – see ",["entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/entry-requirements"],". You will be detained and deported, and your electronic equipment is likely to be confiscated. FCDO does not believe that humanitarian supplies should be delivered in this way. If you send humanitarian assistance or other goods to Gaza, use established channels."]},{"k":"h","s":["Israel-Lebanon"]},{"k":"p","s":["There was an ongoing conflict between Israel and Lebanese Hizballah (LH). On 27 November 2024, LH and Israel agreed to a ceasefire, with a 60-day implementation period. Hostilities resumed in 2026 with a ceasefire agreed on 16 April."]},{"k":"p","s":["There remains a risk that hostilities could reignite, and with little warning. You should check Home Front Command for the latest guidance. Restrictions may be put in place at short notice. If travelling near military operation areas, follow all Israeli official instructions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Military activity continues on the Israel-Lebanon border. Keep up to date with the news while travelling. See also section on Conflict with Lebanese Hizballah."]},{"k":"h","s":["Israel-Syria border"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel within 500m of the border with Syria (the ‘Alpha Line’)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The situation is fragile, with military exchanges either side of the border. If you’re travelling in the area, be aware of your personal security, check local media and follow advice from local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Occupied Golan Heights"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel within 500m of the Area of Separation in the occupied Golan Heights (the ‘Alpha line’). Do not attempt to enter the occupied Golan Heights through Syria."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the Sheba’a Farms and Ghajjar."]},{"k":"p","s":["Following the conflict between Israel and Lebanese Hizballah, a ceasefire was agreed on 27 November. There remains a risk that hostilities could reignite, and with little warning. Check Home Front Command for the latest guidance. In the occupied Golan Heights, restrictions may be put in place at short notice. Rocket attacks and sporadic gunfire occur without warning. There is also a risk of falling debris from Israeli and Syrian air defence systems."]},{"k":"p","s":["Landmines have been planted across the occupied Golan Heights, including near to populated areas and roads. These areas are usually marked and often fenced off. Follow established roads and paths. FCDO long-standing advice has been to not hike off-trail. If you’re in the region, follow advice from local law enforcement."]},{"k":"h","s":["Border with Egypt"]},{"k":"p","s":["The security situation on the border with Egypt is volatile. Take extra care when using the Route 10 road, which runs along the Israeli border with Egypt. Route 10 is sometimes closed by the Israeli authorities. Consider using other routes."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent clashes between Israeli Security Forces and Palestinians in these areas and violent incidents can occur without warning."]},{"k":"h","s":["West Bank"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been a heightened state of tension and violent clashes resulting in deaths in the West Bank since the outbreak of conflict in October 2023."]},{"k":"p","s":["Expect road closures and numerous checkpoints across the West Bank."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are no warning sirens or official air raid shelters inside the West Bank, outside of Israeli settlements."]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot travel into or out of the West Bank without passing through at least one Israeli military checkpoint. You need a passport and immigration slip to go through these checkpoints. Checkpoints may be closed during Jewish high holidays, Israeli public holidays and periods of increased instability restricting movement in and out of the West Bank. This does not normally affect foreign nationals, but would affect British-Palestinian dual nationals. Road closures can occur with little notice. Keep up to date with local travel advice through local media, and international information outlets like the UN’s Access Coordination Unit."]},{"k":"p","s":["The cities of Bethlehem, Ramallah and Jericho see large numbers of tourists including on organised tours, although tourist numbers have reduced since 7 October 2023. While there have been no recent reports of any serious incidents involving foreigners, you should take care when travelling anywhere in the West Bank."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent incidents"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of violent incidents and demonstrations in the West Bank (see ",["Political situation","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/safety-and-security"]," for details). If you are in a location where an Israeli security operation or armed clashes are ongoing, stay inside and wait for the local authorities to confirm that the situation is calm before moving to a different location."]},{"k":"p","s":["Israelis living in the illegal settlements in the West Bank occasionally organise demonstrations which can turn violent. There are reports that settlers have threatened people travelling near to settlements and settlement outposts. Take care if you are near settlements, including those in the hills around Nablus, in the South Hebron hills and settlement outposts."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a closed military zone in the H2 area of Hebron (around Ash-Shuhada Street and the Ibrahimi Mosque/Tomb of the Patriarchs), where there is a risk of a hostile reaction from members of extremist groups."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be particularly cautious if considering a visit to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Hebron or Palestinian refugee camps which have previously been the site of violent clashes – FCDO advises against all travel to the camps in Jenin and Nablus"]},{"k":"li","s":["settlements and settlement outposts where there have been recent violent incidents – for example, near Beit El, Homesh, Shilo, Evyatar"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid these locations after dark."]},{"k":"p","s":["Incidents have also occurred along Route 60 (especially junctions near Nablus), Route 443 and other West Bank arterial roads used by both Palestinians and Israelis. Use extreme caution on these routes, particularly at night, and leave if you see any signs of a disturbance."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Transport in the West Bank"]},{"k":"p","s":["We advise you not to use taxis in the West Bank, because of their involvement in a significant number of accidents."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid using buses in the West Bank and consider the difficulties and risks of travelling between Jerusalem and Ramallah via checkpoints, along Route 60 (especially the junctions near Nablus), Route 443 and other West Bank arterial roads used by both Palestinians and Israelis."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice covers Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["For an ambulance dial:"]},{"k":"li","s":["100 in Israel"]},{"k":"li","s":["101 in the West Bank and Gaza"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Israel","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/110/israel#Vaccine_Recommendations"]," and ",["Palestine","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/173/palestinian#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Israel","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/110/israel#General_Information"]," and ",["Palestine","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/173/palestinian"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["Healthcare in Israel and Palestine is not free and medical treatment can be expensive. Hospitals will insist on payment and may take legal action to stop you leaving until bills are paid. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has lists of ",["medical providers in Israel","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/israel-list-of-medical-facilities"]," and ",["medical providers in Palestine","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-occupied-palestinian-territories-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Israel and Palestine","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/information-for-british-nationals-residing-in-israel-and-the-opts#healthcare-in-israel-and-the-opts"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["This travel advice covers Israel and Palestine."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Israel and Palestine"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 101"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 102"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 100"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["English-speaking lawyers in Israel","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/israel-list-of-lawyers"]," and ",["English-speaking lawyers in Palestine","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-occupied-palestinian-territories-list-of-lawyers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["translators and interpreters in Israel","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/israel-list-of-translators"]," and ",["translators and interpreters in Palestine","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-occupied-palestinian-territories-list-of-lawyers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Israel and Palestine","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-information-israel-the-opts"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Israel","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/israel-prisoner-pack"]," and ",["arrested or imprisoned in Palestine","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/the-occupied-palestinian-territories-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/israel/british-embassy-tel-aviv"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/israel/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers information and advice for ",["British companies operating overseas in Israel","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-israel"]," and ",["British companies operating overseas in Palestine","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-palestinian-territories"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":47545,"change":"Updated information about Regional tensions (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)"},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/jamaica":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"f5ea0b6eecaecae4cd9e8f37c5a64e272ce9bd9e32bc4dd8cf084f642ab15c2f","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/jamaica","bytes":66138,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Jamaica travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-08T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-05-06T12:06:25+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Hurricane Melissa"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hurricane Melissa made landfall as a major hurricane in Jamaica in October 2025. All Western parishes suffered significant damage and some communities are still without electricity and piped water. In the worst affected areas, access to healthcare is limited, and there is still debris and standing water that carries health risks, including water-borne and mosquito-borne diseases."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide and see ",["support for British nationals abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/collections/support-for-british-nationals-abroad"]," for information about specific travel topics."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/jamaica/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Jamaica’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Jamaica set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the Jamaican High Commission in the UK."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Jamaica, your passport must be valid for the duration of your stay. You must have 2 blank pages for entry and exit stamps."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You do not need a visa to visit Jamaica. You will usually be granted entry for up to 90 days. The date you must leave Jamaica is stamped on your passport."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to extend your stay, apply to the ",["Jamaican Passport, Immigration and Citizenship Agency","https://www.pica.gov.jm/"],". If you overstay without authority, you could be fined or arrested."]},{"k":"h","s":["Airport tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["Arrival and departure taxes are usually included in the cost of your ticket. If unsure check with your carrier who will be able to advise you."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Jamaica guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/113/jamaica#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Jamaica","https://www.jacustoms.gov.jm/tags/Travellers"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must make a customs declaration before entering Jamaica. You should complete the ",["Immigration and Custom Form C5","https://enterjamaica.com/"]," online where possible before you arrive."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into Jamaica"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to bring meat and dairy products into Jamaica. Customs officials may search your baggage and will destroy banned foodstuffs."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Jamaica"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 US dollars or more. You must declare this on your C5 form. You will also have to complete the Financial Investigation Division Cross Border Form which will be provided by a customs officer. You will need to provide:"]},{"k":"li","s":["proof of the source of money"]},{"k":"li","s":["the intended use of the funds"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you do not declare money as required, it is a breach of the Jamaican Customs Act. Your money could be seized and you could get a fine."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. You should remain vigilant at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Jamaica"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Jamaica, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Zones of Special Operations"]},{"k":"p","s":["The government can put enhanced security measures in place in response to outbursts of violence and shootings, such as a State of Emergency (SOE) or Zone of Special Operations (ZOSOs). A SOE or ZOSO will have specific boundaries and will temporarily give the police and military additional powers. These can include imposing curfews, cordons, searching of persons, vehicles, and places. Curfews can be imposed with little notice and are usually a short-term measure. Tourists and visitors are not usually affected by SOE or ZOZOs. Check locally whether any security measures or curfews apply and follow the advice of the local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Crowds and demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests and demonstrations occur across Jamaica and can cause significant disruption to traffic and public transportation. Any event with large crowds has the potential to turn violent, including large celebratory gatherings. They can also be used by criminals as cover for robbery and theft. Stay away from areas where protests, demonstrations or marches are taking place. Monitor local and social media updates."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Crime and homicide rates are high in Jamaica. Gang violence and shootings mostly occur in inner city areas. Tourist areas are not usually affected by gang-related crime and violence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious particularly when travelling in and around:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kingston"]},{"k":"li","s":["Spanish Town"]},{"k":"li","s":["Savanna-la-Mar"]},{"k":"li","s":["parts of Montego Bay including Flankers, Barrett Town, Glendevon, Rose Heights and Mount Salem"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["The motive for most attacks on tourists is robbery. Take extra care in more run-down areas and those less visited by tourists."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of your surroundings and:"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not walk in isolated areas or deserted beaches, even during the day"]},{"k":"li","s":["travel with others or go on a tour with a reputable company when possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["be careful when withdrawing money from ATMs. Do not withdraw a lot of money at one time or use ATMs in badly lit areas. It is generally safer to use ATMs during daylight hours"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid using buses at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not display valuables or leave them in your car"]},{"k":"li","s":["consider removing expensive jewellery"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay alert and be wary of people who approach you"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid walking at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that resisting a robbery could lead to a violent response, including the use of weapons, that could result in physical injury"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most hotels and resorts are well guarded, but burglaries can occur. Follow hotel security instructions, use hotel safes for your valuables, including your passport, and lock windows and doors. In residential accommodation ensure that proper locks and window grilles are fitted."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rape and sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some British nationals have reported incidents of rape and sexual assault in tourist areas, including beach resorts. In many cases, the alleged perpetrator was someone the victim met socially, for example at a bar, hotel, beach or excursion."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although incidents are infrequent, simple habits such as increased awareness and extra precaution can greatly reduce risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid isolated areas, particularly at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["use reputable, licenced providers for services and excursions, including taxis. Carry out your own research and consult resort staff/your tour operator."]},{"k":"li","s":["do not disclose personal information, accommodation/ room number or social media accounts to new acquaintances"]},{"k":"li","s":["if traveling solo, tell someone you trust (at home or at the hotel) where you’ll be and always ensure you have transport arrangements in place to get back to your hotel independently"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you experience sexual harassment or assault, or if you feel threatened or unsafe, report it as soon as possible to hotel staff or your tour operator."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also contact:"]},{"k":"li","s":["the ",["British High Commission in Kingston","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-high-commission-jamaica"]," on + 1 (876) 936 0700"]},{"k":"li","s":["the Centre for Investigation of Sexual Offences and Child Abuse (CISOCA). A dedicated police service providing safe and confidential investigative and emotional support to victims, on +1 (876) 926 4079 or use this email address cisoca@jcf.gov.jm"]},{"k":"p","s":["Refer to the ",["advice for women travelling abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]," and our ",["information page for victims of rape and sexual assault","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/rape-and-sexual-assault-in-jamaica-information-for-victims/jamaica-information-for-victims-of-rape-and-sexual-assault"]," for further information."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to smoke marijuana (ganja) in Jamaica. There are penalties for all drug offences including those involving marijuana. For possession of amounts of up to 2 ounces you will get a fine of 500 Jamaican dollars, to be paid within 30 days. Severe penalties apply for all other drug related offences, including attempting to export narcotics."]},{"k":"p","s":["All prison sentences are served in full in Jamaica. Prison conditions are harsh. Always pack your own luggage and do not carry anything through customs for someone else."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Male same-sex sexual activity is illegal, but the law is not always strictly enforced. The attitude of many Jamaicans towards same-sex relationships is hostile. Be mindful of local attitudes and be aware that showing affection in public may receive unwanted attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when using dating apps in Jamaica, especially those used by the LGBT+ community. Criminals have used apps to lure victims to meet in a public place but later assault and rob them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel to and from Norman Manley International Airport"]},{"k":"p","s":["There’s been sporadic violence in recent years in the Mountain View area – one of 2 routes between Kingston and Norman Manley International Airport. Most people take the Humming Bird route via South Camp Road to reduce the risk of being robbed on route."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals have been tracked and robbed when travelling from the airport to their private accommodation. Be cautious when driving and getting out of the car."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Jamaica. If you still have a paper driving licence, you need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"],". Your UK driving licence can be used to drive in Jamaica for up to 6 months."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are unfamiliar with Kingston, do not drive in the city. If you get lost, you and your passengers may be at risk."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Jamaica. If convicted, you may get a fine and possible imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions and driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many roads are badly maintained with poor signage. In some locations a 4-wheel-drive vehicle is recommended. Road accidents and fatalities are common. Roads in rural areas are often narrow and winding and poorly lit at night. Weather conditions can exacerbate poor driving conditions."]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards vary. Lane discipline is poor. Speeding and drink-driving is common. Many drivers do not have car insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drivers and front-seat passengers must wear a seatbelt at all times. However, hire cars and minibuses do not always have rear seatbelts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Motorbike riders must wear a helmet."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxi safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Use Jamaican Tourist Board (JTB) approved taxis and minibuses for excursions, airport transfers and sightseeing. Most hotels and resorts have assigned JTB drivers who carry photo ID and display a blue JTB sticker on the front windscreen. Taxi-hailing apps such as Uber are now available in some areas of the island (including Kingston)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/extreme-weather-and-natural-hazards"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hurricanes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hurricane season is normally from June to November. We are seeing more uncharacteristic weather in Jamaica and the region is increasingly vulnerable to climate change impacts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hurricanes can cause fallen trees, damaged or blocked roads and flooding. Check your route in advance. Exercise caution in areas close to swamps, rivers, gullies and mangroves."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local news and check ",["World Meteorological Association","https://worldweather.wmo.int/en/country.html?countryCode=26"]," weather reports for Jamaica."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["Extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/tropical-cyclones"]," for advice about how to prepare effectively and what to do if you’re likely to be affected by a hurricane."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about what to do before, during and after an earthquake."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 110 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Jamaica","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/113/jamaica#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Jamaica","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/113/jamaica"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Jamaica"]},{"k":"p","s":["The standard of medical facilities – both private and government-operated – varies and may not meet UK standards. Access to healthcare in the areas worst affected by Hurricane Melissa is limited, with some areas still operating field hospitals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Treatment can be expensive with doctors and hospitals expecting immediate cash payment for health services."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Jamaica","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-medical-facilitiespractitioners-in-jamaica"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Jamaica","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-jamaica#healthcare-in-jamaica"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Jamaica"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 110"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 110"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 119"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Jamaica"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Jamaica"]," in Jamaica."]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with ",["a death","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/when-someone-dies-in-jamaica"]," in Jamaica"]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/jamaica-prisoner-pack"]," in Jamaica"]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/jamaica/british-high-commission-kingston"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/jamaica/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Jamaica","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-jamaica"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":15545,"change":"New information on incidents of sexual assault in tourist areas and advice on personal safety measures ('Safety and security' page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/morocco":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"d3076169da3748164d6807f18403c1a1d233812cf11b08f90114e6c4e294a109","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/morocco","bytes":80199,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Morocco travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-15T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-19T12:00:36+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/morocco/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Morocco’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Morocco set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Moroccan Consulate General in the UK","https://www.consulat.ma/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Morocco, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure ",["your passport is not damaged","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/damaged-and-faulty-passports/damaged-british-passports-accessible#definitions-of-damage-or-fraudulent-tampering"],". The Moroccan authorities have denied entry to some travellers with damaged passports. Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Lost or stolen passports"]},{"k":"p","s":["If your passport is lost or stolen, you will need to apply for an emergency travel document from the British embassy. You will also need to show a police report to be able to leave the country. The police will issue a written report, this can be a “déclaration de perte” for a lost passport or a “déclaration de vol” for a stolen passport. Stolen or lost passports must be reported in the city where the theft or loss occurred."]},{"k":"p","s":["Border officials should stamp your passport when you enter Morocco. Some travellers have had difficulties leaving Morocco because their passport did not have an entry stamp."]},{"k":"h","s":["Sending passports by post"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to send passports by post to or through Morocco. The authorities will confiscate British passports sent to or through Morocco by post or courier."]},{"k":"h","s":["Carrying unaccompanied passports"]},{"k":"p","s":["Carrying another person’s passport may attract scrutiny from Police, Immigration, Customs, or Border Officials. Travellers are strongly advised not to carry a passport belonging to an individual who is not accompanying them unless there is a clear and legitimate reason for doing so."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Morocco without a visa for up to 90 days for tourism."]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer than 90 days, you must request an extension at a Moroccan police station."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re going to Morocco for reasons other than tourism, check visa requirements with the ",["Moroccan Consulate General in the UK","https://www.consulat.ma/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Arriving by private boat"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you arrive by private boat, you must enter at a ",["recognised port of entry","https://www.anp.org.ma/en/"],". It is illegal to enter through other ports."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Morocco, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a polio vaccine if you’re coming from a polio-affected country."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Morocco guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/154/morocco#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Morocco","https://www.douane.gov.ma/web/guest/particuliers"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into or out of Morocco"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Moroccan dirham is a closed ‘non-convertible’ currency. This means it cannot be easily exchanged outside Morocco for other currencies ."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must declare foreign currency worth 100,000 Moroccan dirham or more (equal to around £8,000) when you enter or leave the country."]},{"k":"p","s":["Passing fraudulent banknotes carries significant prison sentences. Defacing Moroccan banknotes is also illegal and punishable by imprisonment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Morocco"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are likely to try to carry out attacks in Morocco."]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorism attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["transport hubs"]},{"k":"li","s":["locations popular with tourists and foreigners"]},{"k":"li","s":["government buildings"]},{"k":"li","s":["crowded places"]},{"k":"li","s":["businesses with western interests"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is an increased threat linked to the number of Moroccans sympathetic or belonging to Daesh (formerly ISIL) and other extremist groups. Authorities regularly disrupt terrorist cells."]},{"k":"p","s":["In some places, including hotels and tourists sites, there may be protective security measures, including security guards."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests and demonstrations could occur across the country, particularly in large cities, often without warning. These events are typically monitored closely by law enforcement. While authorised protests are generally peaceful, unauthorised ones have sometimes led to clashes between protesters and police. Such gatherings can cause travel disruption in the affected areas. Avoid political gatherings and demonstrations and follow local news and directions from security officials."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["There can be occasional violent crime in Morocco. Criminals have used knives against tourists in street attacks, thefts and burglaries in major cities and along beaches. To reduce your risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid quiet areas, particularly after dark"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not carry large amounts of money or valuables"]},{"k":"p","s":["Petty crime is common in tourist areas, especially in historical districts (medina quarters) and on beaches. Crimes include:"]},{"k":"li","s":["pickpocketing"]},{"k":"li","s":["bag-snatching"]},{"k":"li","s":["drive-by motorcycle theft of visible jewellery and handbags"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious when asking for directions and using ATMs – aggressive begging is common."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Scams"]},{"k":"p","s":["Credit card fraud and scams are common. Beware of scammers substituting inferior goods for the ones you bought. Remain alert to potential confidence tricks."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bogus tourist guides"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is common for people posing as official tourist guides to harass tourists."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you use a guide in a historical district (medina quarter), make sure they have an official badge and permission from the local authority."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Marriage fraud"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be cautious if you travel to Morocco for a relationship or to find someone you met on the internet. Incidents of marriage fraud and attempted extortion have affected British nationals. Make sure you keep your return ticket, passport and personal belongings safe."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Methanol poisoning"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been deaths and cases of serious illness caused by alcoholic drinks containing methanol in Morocco."]},{"k":"p","s":["Even small amounts of methanol can kill. It is not possible to identify methanol in alcoholic drinks by taste or smell. See ",["Travel Aware Drink Spiking and methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," for information about how to reduce the risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Seek urgent medical attention if you or someone you are travelling with show the ",["signs of methanol poisoning","https://travelaware.campaign.gov.uk/spiking-and-methanol-poisoning/"]," after drinking."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Morocco’s laws and customs are very different to those in the UK and reflect the fact that Morocco is an Islamic country. Always respect local traditions, customs, laws and religions. Make sure your actions do not offend, especially during the holy month of Ramadan or if you plan to visit religious areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ramadan"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ramadan is a holy month for Muslims. The dates vary by year and country, next starting in February 2027. During this time, eating or drinking, swearing, smoking or chewing gum in public in the daytime may cause offence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Get more advice when you arrive from your tour guide, hotel or business contacts, where applicable. You should also:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check opening hours of shops and restaurants"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that hotels and restaurants serving food or drink in fasting hours may separate you from Muslim guests, for example with screens"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow local dress codes – clothing that does not meet local dress codes may cause more offence at this time"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that fasting can cause tiredness, particularly during the later afternoon and early evening"]},{"k":"li","s":["be patient and show tolerance"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware that driving may be erratic, particularly when people are trying to get home at dusk."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Laws against religious conversion"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to attempt to convert a Muslim to another faith and to distribute evangelical literature (such as Arabic-language bibles). Attempting to convert a Muslim to another faith can result in fines or up to 3 years’ imprisonment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public criticism of Islam, including in speeches, print or online media, can result in heavy fines and up 2 years’ imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual relations outside of marriage"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sexual activity between unmarried people and adultery are illegal for Moroccan nationals – this includes sharing a hotel room, particularly with foreign nationals."]},{"k":"p","s":["The law regarding unmarried people sharing a hotel room does not generally apply to visiting foreign nationals, particularly in popular tourist areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid showing affection in public, particularly near religious sites as well as in tourist areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Using dating applications in Morocco may break laws relating to sexual relations outside of marriage. Be aware of the legal and personal safety risks when using these applications."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual relations are illegal in Morocco. Showing affection in public can lead to prosecution. Meeting people through online applications, can carry legal, personal safety and privacy risks."]},{"k":"p","s":["See more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["Alcohol is available in licensed venues. However, drinking alcohol in the street and anywhere other than a licensed restaurant or bar is illegal and can lead to arrest. Travellers should respect local laws and customs at all times."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Morocco has a zero-tolerance approach towards drugs. Possessing, using or trafficking illegal drugs, including cannabis, are serious offences and carry severe penalties."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for these actions, including when transiting through the country. Airports in Morocco are equipped with technology and security for detecting items prohibited by customs controls, including for the baggage or transiting passengers. Do not accept items from strangers or leave your bags attended."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Women travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Women may receive unwanted attention in Morocco, especially when travelling alone. Consider wearing loose-fitting clothing which cover the arms, legs and chest. See ",["advice for woman travellers abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Photography and Filming"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to take photographs near sensitive political or military sites. Always ask permission before taking pictures of people, especially children."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pornography"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to possess pornographic material. This includes printed and digital material, and any type of material contrary to Moroccan laws related to morality and public order."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flying drones"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to bring a drone to Morocco, you must get permission from the ",["Directorate General for Civil Aviation","https://www.aviationcivile.gov.ma/"]," (in French) to fly a drone. If you do not, you risk fines and confiscation of your equipment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Morocco, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both the ",["1968 version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel. Morocco no longer accepts the 1949 version of the IDP."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you stay longer than one year, you need a ",["Moroccan driving licence","https://consulat.ma/en/driving-license"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get a ",["green card from your insurer","https://www.gov.uk/vehicle-insurance/driving-abroad"]," and carry it with you to prove you have the minimum insurance cover in Morocco."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have strict requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience and a higher minimum age."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Morocco. If you are tested and found to have any alcohol in your system, you will get a fine and possible imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be more alert to other vehicles, pedestrians and animals as poor lighting can make it dangerous to drive at night. When weather conditions are poor, secondary routes and mountain roads can be especially hazardous. On motorways, be cautious of overloaded lorries and trucks overtaking when there is no hard shoulder."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road accidents"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road accidents are a frequent occurrence in Morocco. If you’re involved in a road accident, complete a form (‘constat amiable’), to be signed by both parties. Blank forms are available from insurance company booths in Tangier Port and tobacconists in all cities."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are involved in a fatal road accident, and the Moroccan authorities think you’re responsible, they may detain you before a trial hearing."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Vehicle documentation"]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities will record your registration number when you drive into Morocco. If you’re not in the same vehicle when you try to leave the country, they will detain you and refuse to let you exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to show evidence of motor insurance when entering and exiting the country. Always carry your insurance, licence and registration documents with you when driving."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many taxis booked through ride sharing applications may be unregulated and unlicensed. Travellers should therefore exercise caution and remain vigilant if using these applications. Drivers may not be registered with the authorities, and their vehicles may not be insured to carry passengers. The police may tell you to get out of an unlicensed taxi if they stop it. It is advisable to either agree a fare in advance or check the taxi is using a meter."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drivers of ‘petits’ or ‘grands taxis’ sometimes speed and do not follow other driving rules, particularly in big cities. Exercise caution when using petit taxis, especially during late night journeys. Be aware that petit taxi drivers will often pick up other customers during the journey. Should you feel uncomfortable at any point, end the journey as soon as it is safe to do so and move to a well-lit area."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Electronic scooters and bikes"]},{"k":"p","s":["When riding an electronic scooter or bike, wear a helmet and do not use headphones or earphones while riding. Be aware there are often no cycle lanes on roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow local laws and regulations and ensure you are aware of any requirements before using an electric scooter."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["Providers of recreational and adventure tourism may not meet UK safety standards. Check safety standards with the tour operators or providers and make sure you are insured if you take part in activities such as water sports, boat tours or quad biking. Be aware that some insurance policies will not cover these activities. Book excursions for activities and water sports through reputable agents or at your hotel or resort."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking in the Atlas Mountains"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to hike in the Atlas Mountains:"]},{"k":"li","s":["research trails and understand how much experience you’ll need"]},{"k":"li","s":["pack essentials such as water, sunscreen and appropriate clothing"]},{"k":"li","s":["hire a professional guide"]},{"k":"li","s":["get comprehensive travel insurance and make sure it covers your planned activities"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Quad biking"]},{"k":"p","s":["Quad bike accidents involving British nationals frequently occur in resort areas. Take the same precautions as you would in the UK. Safety standards vary considerably. Always wear a crash helmet."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hot air balloons"]},{"k":"p","s":["Book hot air balloon trips only through licensed tour operators. Unlicensed providers may not meet required safety standards."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Beaches"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many beaches in Morocco have limited or no lifeguard cover, and safety signage may be minimal. Strong currents and unexpected waves can occur. Take care when entering the water and avoid swimming in isolated areas. See ",["water safety guidance if swimming","https://www.abta.com/tips-and-advice/staying-safe-on-holiday/swim-safe"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Swimming in open water, including dams and rivers, can be dangerous. Deep mud and steep underwater slopes can trap people and lead to drowning."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes are a risk in Morocco. The last major earthquake, in 2023, killed almost 3,000 people. There are occasional minor earthquakes. Familiarise yourself with earthquake safety procedures and any instructions in hotel rooms."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the event of an earthquake, stay away from walls, windows, trees, signs. It is safer to stand in open spaces or shelter under heavy furniture or in a door threshold. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Heavy rain can cause flash flooding in some areas, particularly in the mountains or near rivers during winter months. Walking and driving can be dangerous in flooded areas. If you’re near a flood, monitor local media and follow instructions from local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of wildfires during the summer season. Wildfires are highly dangerous and unpredictable. The situation can change quickly. Always follow the advice and instructions of the local authorities. Make sure cigarettes are properly extinguished, do not light barbecues and do not leave empty glass bottles behind."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Morocco. It only covers regions where the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/morocco"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/morocco/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Western Sahara"]},{"k":"p","s":["Western Sahara is a disputed territory. If you’re in Western Sahara and need emergency help from the UK government, contact the British Embassy in Rabat, Morocco, who provide consular assistance for Western Sahara. See ",["Western Sahara travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/western-sahara"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Morocco-Algeria border"]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities have closed land and sea borders between Morocco and Algeria. They patrol and closely monitor them. Do not attempt to cross the border – it is illegal to cross without authorisation."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are in a boat or jet ski, make sure you:"]},{"k":"li","s":["know where the border is"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay within Moroccan waters"]},{"k":"li","s":["have enough fuel to return to shore"]},{"k":"p","s":["People entering Algerian waters illegally are likely to be intercepted and investigated."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have appropriate travel insurance for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 150 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Morocco","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/154/morocco#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Morocco","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/154/morocco"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Morocco. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Henna tattoos"]},{"k":"p","s":["Henna tattoos can cause a painful allergic reaction including swelling and an itchy rash in some people."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Rabies"]},{"k":"p","s":["Rabies and other animal-borne diseases are present in Morocco. Stray animals are common in many towns and cities. Packs of dogs often gather in parks, on wasteland, and in quieter areas, and can behave aggressively. Do not approach or feed stray animals. If you are bitten or scratched, seek medical advice immediately."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have prescription medication issued in the UK, ensure you bring an adequate supply for the duration of your trip and plan carefully to avoid running out. On some occasions, travellers have struggled to source medication."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you require medication in Morocco, contact the nearest pharmacy. If they do not have your medication, they will ask you to get another prescription from a Moroccan doctor for an alternative medication. Pharmacies are open 24 hours in every city and district."]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Food hygiene and allergies"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers to Morocco should follow good food and water hygiene to reduce the risk of stomach bugs. Travellers who fall ill are advised to seek medical help if symptoms, such as vomiting and diarrhoea, do not improve after a few days."]},{"k":"p","s":["Travellers with allergies should take extra care when dining in Morocco. Allergen information is not consistently provided, and cross-contamination risks may be higher than in the UK. Make your allergies clear and avoid foods you are unsure about."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Morocco"]},{"k":"p","s":["Public health facilities in Morocco provide limited medical care. Private clinics are available and operate to a higher standard. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Morocco","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/morocco-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Morocco"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 150"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 150"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 190"]},{"k":"p","s":["Gendarmerie (military police): 177"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides guidance on how to help yourself stay safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Morocco"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Morocco"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Morocco"]," in Morocco"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Morocco","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/morocco-bereavement-information-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Morocco","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/morocco-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help ",["if you’re a victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if ",["you’re in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["if you are affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/morocco/british-embassy-rabat"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/morocco/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Morocco","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-morocco"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":23718,"change":"This travel advice has been reviewed for accuracy with updates made throughout, including new information about passports, using dating applications, outdoor activities and adventure tourism, using electronic scooters and bikes, quad biking, hot air balloons and beaches and wildfires; information ab"},"https://theconversation.com/could-these-bacteria-killing-viruses-help-fight-antibiotic-resistance-a-new-discovery-takes-us-closer-295748":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"9d94557db53505fcc2240cfb09b62e433beb5cbe50431f1d1eab56bb67a1cc47","read":"https://theconversation.com/could-these-bacteria-killing-viruses-help-fight-antibiotic-resistance-a-new-discovery-takes-us-closer-295748","bytes":185444,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Could these bacteria-killing viruses help fight antibiotic resistance? A new discovery takes us closer","by":[{"n":"Manuela Fuchs","r":"Postdoctoral Researcher, Department of Microbiology, University of Otago"},{"n":"Leah Smith","r":"Research Fellow in Microbiology, University of Otago"},{"n":"Natalie Kyte","r":"Postdoctoral Researcher, Interfaculty Institute of Microbiology & Infection Medicine Tübingen, University of Tübingen"}],"pub":"2026-11-09T18:37:17Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["With their spindly legs and geometric heads, they look more like miniature spacecraft than anything living on Earth. But ",["bacteriophages","https://theconversation.com/bacteriophages-meet-the-viruses-that-hunt-superbugs-278440"],", or simply phages, are among the most abundant biological entities on the planet."]},{"k":"p","s":["These microscopic agents are viruses that can infect and kill bacteria, offering an intriguing alternative to antibiotics at a time that ",["drug-resistant infections are threatening global health","https://theconversation.com/antibiotic-resistance-is-a-growing-problem-but-solutions-do-exist-expert-qanda-286487"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite decades of research, however, scientists still know surprisingly little about how most phages work. Many of their genes have functions that remain a mystery, limiting their potential in medicine and elsewhere."]},{"k":"p","s":["Now, ",["our new research","https://www.nature.com/articles/s41564-026-02486-1"]," offers a way to investigate them in greater detail. We’ve developed a method to pinpoint which genes phages need to function, and to insert new genetic material into their genomes within days."]},{"k":"p","s":["This might eventually help researchers engineer phages that are better at attacking harmful bacteria – opening up possibilities for treating infections that conventional antibiotics struggle against."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why phages are making a comeback"]},{"k":"p","s":["Long before antibiotics became the standard treatment for bacterial infections, doctors were using phages to fight them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Phages were first used in this way a century ago. But with the arrival of antibiotics, ",["inconsistent results","https://www.annualreviews.org/content/journals/10.1146/annurev-virology-100422-040919"]," from early phage treatments and the onset of the Cold War, their medical use declined in Western countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["In ",["his 1945 Nobel Prize lecture","https://www.nobelprize.org/prizes/medicine/1945/fleming/lecture/"],", Alexander Fleming, who discovered penicillin, warned that bacteria could develop resistance to antibiotics. His warning proved prescient."]},{"k":"p","s":["As new antibiotics were developed, ",["resistant bacteria emerged","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1369527419300190"],", helped by the overuse and misuse of these drugs. Today, antibiotic resistance ",["is projected to contribute","https://www.thelancet.com/journals/lancet/article/PIIS0140-6736(24)01867-1/fulltext&sa=D&source=docs&ust=1793677091282379&usg=AOvVaw1N4ehsV1rJJp_xGLNS5tsb"]," to more than eight million deaths annually by 2050, prompting renewed interest in phage-based treatments."]},{"k":"p","s":["Despite their growing use in medicine and agriculture, much of what we know about phages comes from a small number of well-studied examples. Their vast diversity, and the functions of many of their genes, ",["remain largely unexplored","https://journals.asm.org/doi/10.1128/mbio.03254-25"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Like humans, phages have genomes containing genes that carry instructions for making proteins. These proteins determine how the viruses function, including how they infect bacteria and reproduce."]},{"k":"p","s":["To investigate phage gene function, scientists need tools that can boost our understanding and turn new knowledge into practical applications."]},{"k":"h","s":["Bridging the knowledge gap"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Current methods","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0167779922002268?via%3Dihub"]," for studying and modifying phages can be time-consuming, work only with certain bacteria, or require detailed knowledge of the phage’s genome."]},{"k":"p","s":["We wanted to overcome these limitations by developing a method that could work across different phages and their bacterial hosts. To do this, we harnessed ",["transposons","https://www.nature.com/scitable/topicpage/transposons-the-jumping-genes-518/"]," – mobile pieces of DNA that insert themselves into random positions in a genome and disrupt gene function."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our approach, called Phage Tn-seq (transposon sequencing), combines these insertions with DNA sequencing, allowing us to pinpoint where mutations occur and how they affect the phage."]},{"k":"p","s":["Since the late 2000s, similar techniques have helped scientists understand ",["bacterial gene function","https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC7291929/"],". Typically, transposons carry an antibiotic resistance gene, allowing bacteria that receive them to survive antibiotic treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["But this doesn’t work directly with phages, which aren’t affected by antibiotics. Instead, we exploited what has been described as a molecular “ ",["arms race","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/31942051/"],"” between bacteria and the phages that infect them."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bacteria have evolved ",["CRISPR-Cas immune systems","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0300908415001042"],", which recognise and cut up invading viral DNA, to defend themselves against phages. In turn, some phages have developed anti-CRISPR proteins that overcome these defences."]},{"k":"p","s":["We used one of these proteins, carried on the transposon, instead of an antibiotic resistance gene. By applying CRISPR-Cas selection, we could eliminate phages that hadn’t received the transposon. This left us with a pool of phages carrying different mutations, which we could study to identify the function of their genes."]},{"k":"p","s":["Disrupting a phage gene might have no noticeable effect, reduce the phage’s ability to function, or prevent it from replicating. By sequencing the DNA, we can locate these mutations and see which ones are rare or absent."]},{"k":"p","s":["These gaps tell us which genes are essential for the phage to reproduce, allowing us to map the genes it needs to successfully infect bacteria."]},{"k":"h","s":["Building better phages"]},{"k":"p","s":["Having developed a way to identify which genes phages need, we wanted to see whether the same technique could give them new abilities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our method automatically selects phages that survive transposon insertion. We tested whether we could use this process to introduce additional “cargo” genes into their genomes."]},{"k":"p","s":["We then added a gene encoding ",["green fluorescent protein","https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9759496/"],", causing infected bacterial cells to glow bright green under a microscope. While this served as a demonstration, the technique could potentially introduce genes that make phages more effective at killing bacteria."]},{"k":"p","s":["In this space, one promising application involves ",["biofilms","https://www.nature.com/articles/s41522-025-00875-8"]," – communities of bacteria that clump together inside protective, sugar-based shells, making infections difficult to treat with antibiotics."]},{"k":"p","s":["Using Phage Tn-seq, researchers ",["might engineer phages to produce proteins","https://www.pnas.org/doi/10.1073/pnas.0704624104"]," that break down these layers while attacking the bacteria themselves. This could also make antibiotics, often used alongside phages, more effective."]},{"k":"p","s":["Several countries, including the United States and some European Union members, have introduced programmes offering personalised phage therapy to ",["selected patients","https://www.nature.com/articles/s41467-025-64608-3"],", sometimes using ",["genetically modified phages","https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6557439/"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In New Zealand, however, phage therapy ",["is not routinely available","https://www.rnz.co.nz/national/programmes/ninetonoon/audio/2018992858/otago-scientist-explores-experimental-phage-therapy"]," as a treatment option, partly because of regulatory hurdles and gaps in our understanding of these viruses."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our research won’t overcome those barriers overnight. But by giving scientists new tools to understand and modify phages, it could lay the groundwork for a wider range of applications."]}],"chars":5982},"https://theconversation.com/americas-2-party-system-seems-weird-but-adding-a-3rd-party-could-make-voter-representation-worse-294341":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"13cbb8a096abfa9949b43a63810739464cd9a032e19dce9878b852987d583d94","read":"https://theconversation.com/americas-2-party-system-seems-weird-but-adding-a-3rd-party-could-make-voter-representation-worse-294341","bytes":182544,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"America’s 2-party system seems weird, but adding a 3rd party could make voter representation worse","by":[{"n":"Robin E. Best","r":"Professor of Political Science, Binghamton University, State University of New York"}],"pub":"2026-11-10T13:36:00Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In most races in the ",["midterm elections","https://theconversation.com/topics/2026-midterm-elections-178375"]," on Nov. 3, 2026, Americans had only two realistic choices: Democrats and Republicans."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a ",["scholar of parties and elections","https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=RgFLj50AAAAJ&hl=en"],", I am often asked why the U.S. has only two major parties, while other democracies offer voters three, four or even five choices. The U.S. system looks weird compared to those, but that isn’t necessarily a bad thing."]},{"k":"p","s":["The two “umbrella” Democratic and Republican parties mask many underlying differences in political preferences, but this large and fluid two-party system may represent voters at least as well as Canada and the United Kingdom do. Those countries elect members of their lower legislative house in the same way as the U.S., but, ",["as my research suggests","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.electstud.2009.07.006"],", their additional parties can distort representation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Winner takes all"]},{"k":"p","s":[["An electoral system","https://www.bloomsbury.com/us/electoral-systems-9781350348950/"]," is the set of rules that determine how votes translate into elected representatives. The U.S. uses what’s called a ",["single-member district plurality","https://www.congress.gov/crs-product/IF12567"],", or an SMD-p system, which means each district elects only one representative, and whoever gets the most votes wins."]},{"k":"p","s":["This “winner-take-all” system is different from proportional representation, the electoral system used by most other democracies. In that system, several representatives are elected in each district, and a party’s share of seats roughly matches its share of the vote – for example, a party winning 40% of the votes would get around 40% of the seats."]},{"k":"p","s":[["SMD-p systems encourage stiff competition","https://doi.org/10.2307/1962968"]," between two parties ",["in each district","https://doi.org/10.1017/CBO9781139174954"],". Because the system gives losing parties nothing, it discourages voters from supporting ",["third parties that have no chance of winning","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.electstud.2015.09.010"],". There is no rule against having more than two parties, but why vote for a party that is sure to lose? With only one possible winner in each district, there are typically only two real competitors."]},{"k":"h","s":["2 parties, many factions"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are ",["many possible reasons","https://doi.org/10.1017/psrm.2015.48"]," the U.S. does not have a viable third party. The presidency pushes politicians to run under one of the major labels, and ",["state ballot access laws","https://www.reuters.com/world/us/how-us-states-make-it-tough-third-parties-elections-2024-01-18/"]," make it harder for minor-party candidates to get on the ballot."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another reason is the nature of the two parties themselves."]},{"k":"p","s":["As “umbrella” parties, the Democrats and Republicans ",["mask underlying differences","https://www.routledge.com/Two-Parties--or-More-The-American-Party-System/Bibby-Maisel/p/book/9780813340319"]," in political preferences. For example, the Pew Research Center identifies ",["nine ideological subtypes of American voters","https://www.pewresearch.org/politics/2026/06/10/how-the-political-typology-groups-feel-about-the-republican-and-democratic-parties/"],", including Faith First Conservatives, Pragmatic and Polite Right, Loyal Liberals and Leftward Progressives."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a different country, with different electoral rules, these nine groups could form multiple political parties. In the U.S., they must choose between Republicans and Democrats. Democrats, for example, unite what Pew calls the Order and Opportunity Left, the Left-Out Left, the Loyal Liberals and the Leftward Progressives."]},{"k":"p","s":["The same umbrella effect shows up in Congress."]},{"k":"p","s":["Congressional Democrats and Republicans have typically had ",["lower levels of party unity","https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1540-5907.2007.00239.x"]," – the extent to which party members vote the same way on legislation – than their European counterparts. This lack of unity is often viewed negatively. In the 1950s, a group of political scientists representing the American Political Science Association, frustrated with how fluid the parties’ positions could be, ",["called for more unified ones","https://doi.org/10.2307/1950997"]," that would provide voters with clear and consistent options."]},{"k":"p","s":["But low unity has an upside: It gives politicians the flexibility to represent their own voters, even when those voters disagree with the rest of the party."]},{"k":"h","s":["More parties, less representation"]},{"k":"p","s":["So why not add another party or two to the American system?"]},{"k":"p","s":["One metric political scientists use to evaluate representation is ",["electoral disproportionality","https://doi.org/10.1016/0261-3794(91)90004-C"],": the gap between parties’ vote shares and their seat shares."]},{"k":"p","s":["The U.S. electoral system is one of the most disproportional that democracies use, since only the district winner is represented. But that disproportionality rarely shows up when only two parties compete."]},{"k":"p","s":["On the other hand, other democracies using the same kind of electoral system as the U.S., such as Canada and the U.K., have several parties competing, which sometimes poses problems for good representation."]},{"k":"p","s":["One example of this was the ",["U.K.’s 2024 general election","https://commonslibrary.parliament.uk/research-briefings/cbp-10009/"],", which produced some of the most disproportional results in British history. Multiparty competition allowed the Labour Party to win more than 63% of the seats in the House of Commons with less than 34% of the vote. Meanwhile, Reform UK received 14% of the vote and won less than 1% of seats."]},{"k":"p","s":["How can this happen?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Imagine a country with 10 districts, each electing one legislator. Only two parties run: the Purple Party and the Yellow Party."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Purple Party wins six districts and Yellow wins four. Purple gets about 56% of the vote and takes 60% of the seats. Yellow gets about 44% of the vote and takes 40% of the seats. In each case, the gap between vote share and seat share is about 4 points. That is considered the measure of disproportionality."]},{"k":"p","s":["Now imagine a third party, the Green Party, enters the race. It wins 30% of the vote in each district, taking more votes from the Purple Party than from Yellow. That costs Purple any districts it had previously won narrowly. Now, Yellow wins six districts and Purple wins four."]},{"k":"p","s":["Three things happen when the third party enters the race."]},{"k":"p","s":["First, the winning party changes. Now, the Yellow Party wins a majority of seats – 60% – with just over a third of the vote."]},{"k":"p","s":["Second, despite receiving 30% of the vote across all districts, and often coming in second place, the Green Party does not win any seats at all."]},{"k":"p","s":["Third, disproportionality increases from 4 points to 28. Only Purple, with 40% of the seats on just under 36% of the vote, comes close to proportionality."]},{"k":"p","s":["Adding a third party flips the winning party from one to the other and increases disproportionality, and this all happens without that third party winning a single seat."]},{"k":"p","s":[["My research suggests","https://doi.org/10.1016/j.electstud.2009.07.006"]," that in countries using the SMD-p system, ",["growing support for third parties","https://doi.org/10.1017/gov.2013.16"]," has increased disproportionality, sometimes dramatically. The U.S. is the exception: Its two-party system keeps disproportionality low, often even lower than in ",["countries that use proportional representation","https://worldpopulationreview.com/country-rankings/gallagher-index-by-country"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Changing the rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["The large and fluid two-party system in the U.S. may represent voters at least as well as systems with viable third parties. The only way out without further distorting representation would be to ",["change the electoral system","https://books.google.com/books?hl=en&lr=&id=_FO_DwAAQBAJ&oi=fnd&pg=PP1&dq=american+two-party+system&ots=27H4o2KIl3&sig=Cor-Xzx2MMGWIdkqU2leVPnkqWQ#v=onepage&q=american%20two-party%20system&f=fals"]," to some version of proportional representation. Nothing in the Constitution prevents that."]},{"k":"p","s":["Americans have valid complaints about their parties, and there are ",["ways to address them","https://apsanet.org/Portals/54/reports/APSA-PD%20Political%20Parties%20Report%20%5BFINAL%5D.pdf?ver=wqYXermQIWhy2vB-4zy2vQ%3d%3d"],". But simply adding more parties to the mix is unlikely to solve anything."]}],"chars":6670},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/zambia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:32Z","sha":"9bb778a9280edbbe5eb182050e8a4627730f75f393980480509c0bb1e87252e4","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/zambia","bytes":57555,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Zambia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-18T15:51:00+00:00","mod":"2026-06-01T14:58:33+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/zambia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Zambia’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Zambia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Zambian High Commission in the UK","https://www.facebook.com/zhclondon/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Zambia, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive. It must have at least 2 blank pages for entry stamping."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationality"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Zambia recognises dual nationality. However, to avoid delays at the airport you should leave Zambia on the same passport you used to enter."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["British passport holders do not need a visa to enter Zambia. You must be able to show:"]},{"k":"li","s":["valid return or onward tickets"]},{"k":"li","s":["enough money for your stay"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists may remain in Zambia for a total of 90 days in any 12 month period. For business visitors the maximum stay in Zambia over a 12 month period is 30 days."]},{"k":"p","s":["For further information, email the Zambian High Commission at info@zambiahc.org.uk or contact the ",["Zambian Department of Immigration","https://www.zambiaimmigration.gov.zm/"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["KAZA UNIVISA"]},{"k":"p","s":["The ",["KAZA UNIVISA,","https://www.zambiaimmigration.gov.zm/kaza-univisa/"]," for use in the Kavango Zambezi Transfrontier Conservation Area, is valid for unlimited travel between Zambia and Zimbabwe and for day trips to Botswana. It costs 50 US dollars and is valid for 30 days."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can ",["apply online in advance","https://eservices.zambiaimmigration.gov.zm/"],", or get the visa on arrival if you are arriving at:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Kenneth Kaunda International Airport, Lusaka"]},{"k":"li","s":["Harry Mwanga Nkumbula International Airport, Livingstone"]},{"k":"li","s":["by land at Livingstone, Victoria Falls (Zambia-Zimbabwe border)"]},{"k":"li","s":["by land at Kazungula (Zambia-Botswana border)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Departure tax"]},{"k":"p","s":["On leaving Zambia, all air passengers must pay the equivalent to 25 US dollars for international travel and a security charge of 3 US dollars for domestic travel. Both charges are normally included in the cost of an air ticket, but you will have to pay in cash with Zambian kwacha if they are not."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Zambia, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Zambia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/247/zambia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ebola"]},{"k":"p","s":["As a public health measure, Zambia may introduce entry restrictions including health screening for travellers arriving from affected regions. ",["Check entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice"]," for the country you’re travelling to or transiting."]},{"k":"p","s":["The World Health Organisation (WHO) have ",["declared Ebola as a Public Health Emergency of International Concern","https://www.who.int/news/item/17-05-2026-epidemic-of-ebola-disease-in-the-democratic-republic-of-the-congo-and-uganda-determined-a-public-health-emergency-of-international-concern"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Zambia","https://www.zra.org.zm/importation-of-goods/"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Zambia","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/zambia/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Zambia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorist attacks in Zambia cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places visited by foreigners."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are occasionally demonstrations and protests in Lusaka and other urban areas. They can disrupt local transport and become violent. Avoid them and leave the scene as soon as possible if a crowd develops. Do not cross protester roadblocks as this is likely to provoke a violent reaction from demonstrators."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travel in larger cities and the major game parks is generally safe during daylight hours. However, serious crimes can happen. Pre-arrange transport to avoid walking at night and stay aware of your surroundings, especially after dark. Stay alert and take precautions against vehicle crime by:"]},{"k":"li","s":["keeping windows closed and doors locked when travelling"]},{"k":"li","s":["ignoring hitchhikers or anyone trying to flag you down"]},{"k":"li","s":["watching out for potential carjackers when approaching locked gateways at night, or if an object has been placed to block the road"]},{"k":"li","s":["only using cars arranged for you by a hotel or tour operator"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep valuables and originals of important documents in a safe place and carry a copy of your passport’s photo page and entry stamp."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pornography laws"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to possess pornographic material in Zambia, and offenders may be jailed or deported."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to possess or use drugs, including marijuana. Drug use and smuggling are serious offences."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s illegal to take pictures of sensitive sites such as army barracks or government buildings, and you could be arrested. If in doubt, do not take pictures."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is illegal in Zambia, and anyone convicted can get a long prison sentence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to buy, sell, kill or capture any protected wild animal or trade its parts without a licence. Anyone caught purchasing or trafficking such goods will be prosecuted and get a fine or a prison sentence."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["Wild animals in the bush, including venomous snakes, are unpredictable and do kill. Whether you are travelling on land or water, you are at risk of potentially fatal animal attacks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Adventure sports, including in the Victoria Falls area, carry risks. There have been serious accidents and deaths. The quality of medical care varies greatly. Follow safety instructions closely. Make sure you have appropriate travel insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment or potential repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Zambia, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Zambia for up to 90 days. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"],". If you plan to stay in Zambia for more than 90 days, you’ll need to have the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," or a Zambian driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hire car companies often have stricter requirements for their customers, such as a year of driving experience, a higher minimum age and holding an IDP."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions and driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many roads are severely potholed. During the rainy season from November to April, sudden floods can wash away bridges and roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["Vehicles in Zambia are often inadequately maintained and badly driven. There are frequent fatal crashes. Drink-driving and driving while on a mobile are illegal but commonplace. Zambia’s Road Traffic and Safety Agency prosecutes traffic offenders through a fast-track court system."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is dangerous to drive outside the main towns after dark due to abandoned vehicles, pedestrians and stray animals on the road, and vehicles being driven without lights."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Buses and minibuses"]},{"k":"p","s":["Travel by long-distance public transport can be dangerous due to poor standards of driving, lack of rest periods for drivers, the poor quality of vehicles and poor road conditions. Minibuses in urban areas are usually severely overcrowded, poorly maintained and badly driven."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Zambia. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/zambia"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/zambia/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Zambia-DRC border"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take care when travelling in rural parts of Zambia, close to the border with the Democratic Republic of Congo (DRC). The border is not demarcated and there is a risk of inadvertently illegally entering DRC."]},{"k":"p","s":["Legitimate border crossings in these areas are generally safe."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Zambia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/247/zambia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Zambia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/247/zambia"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["yellow fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue fever"]},{"k":"li","s":["cholera"]},{"k":"li","s":["mpox"]},{"k":"p","s":["The UNAIDS Zambia country progress report of 2020 estimated the overall HIV prevalence in the adult population is 11%, compared to a prevalence of 0.2% in adults in the UK. Take normal precautions to ",["avoid exposure to HIV/AIDS","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/15/sexually-transmitted-infections"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Potential health risks from heavy metals in water"]},{"k":"p","s":["Chemical waste containing heavy metals was released from a mine in Copperbelt Province into the Chambishi Stream and the Mwambashi and Kafue Rivers in February 2025. Exposure to heavy metal contaminants may affect health. As a precaution:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid bathing in rivers and streams near the Chambishi stream, and where the Mwambashi and Kafue rivers meet"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid consuming untreated locally sourced water or fish from this area. Boiling water does not remove heavy metal contaminants"]},{"k":"li","s":["seek medical attention if you feel unwell"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Zambia"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Zambia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/zambia-medical-services/zambia-list-of-medical-facilities-and-practitioners"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Medical facilities throughout Zambia are of a lower standard than in the UK. Facilities in rural areas are basic and emergency services are limited. Carry basic medical supplies. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Zambia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 991"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 992"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 993"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Zambia"]," and ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Zambia"]," in Zambia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Zambia","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/what-to-do-after-a-british-person-dies-in-zambia"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Zambia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/zambia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/zambia/british-high-commission-lusaka"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/zambia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Zambia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-zambia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":13216,"change":"New information about entry requirements for those entering from Ebola-affected regions ('Entry requirements' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/myanmar-genocide-ruling-is-a-watershed-moment-in-international-justice-with-huge-ramifications-for-other-cases-296987":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-19T18:37Z","sha":"f0009eeb827b9452943c8bf1aa20da8711e0e8559ecbd544bcaa9d332e075612","read":"https://theconversation.com/myanmar-genocide-ruling-is-a-watershed-moment-in-international-justice-with-huge-ramifications-for-other-cases-296987","bytes":191435,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Myanmar genocide ruling is a watershed moment in international justice – with huge ramifications for other cases","by":[{"n":"Max Pensky","r":"Co-Director, Institute for Genocide and Mass Atrocity Prevention, Binghamton University, State University of New York"}],"pub":"2026-11-19T17:06:27Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The International Court of Justice’s ",["historic ruling of genocide","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/nov/19/genocide-rohingya-international-court-of-justice-ruling-myanmar"]," against Myanmar on Nov. 19, 2026, will have significant consequences for the parties involved in the case – and potentially some who are not."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Hague’s highly anticipated judgment in ",["Gambia v. Myanmar","https://www.icj-cij.org/case/178"]," is a major victory for Gambia, the tiny west African nation that filed a complaint with the court against Myanmar in 2019. It is also a major moment of accountability for the military leadership of Myanmar."]},{"k":"p","s":["But as an ",["expert in genocide","https://www.binghamton.edu/apps/directory/person/profile/mpensky"]," and mass atrocity prevention, I believe the ruling goes far beyond these nations. Indeed, it is also a watershed moment for international legal justice that is bound to have important effects on the court’s other ongoing genocide cases, particularly the case of ",["South Africa v. Israel","https://www.icj-cij.org/case/192"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["What the court ruled"]},{"k":"p","s":["Gambia’s case focused on actions that Myanmar’s military government called “clearance operations” in the course of its decades-long violent persecution of the country’s ",["Muslim Rohingya minority","https://www.nationalgeographic.com/culture/article/rohingya-people"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["The Tatmadaw","https://www.bbc.com/news/world-asia-56660483"],", as the Myanmar military is known, justified these actions as a counterinsurgency operation. Yet in the course of those attacks, soldiers were found to have ",["destroyed hundreds of Rohingya villages","https://www.amnesty.org/en/latest/press-release/2017/09/who-are-the-rohingya-and-why-are-they-fleeing-myanmar/"],", and to have committed widespread rapes, torture and summary killings."]},{"k":"p","s":["While the precise death toll of the 2017 attacks may never be known, at least 10,000 Rohingya civilians ",["are thought to have died","https://www.cbc.ca/news/world/hague-icj-court-myanmar-rohingya-ruling-9.7427764"],", and roughly 750,000 Rohingya fled to neighboring Bangladesh. There they joined other Rohingya in what is now the ",["world’s largest refugee camp","https://www.unhcr.org/where-we-work/countries/bangladesh"]," of over 1.2 million people, comprised of those who had already fled years of the Myanmar government’s persecution and attacks."]},{"k":"p","s":["The court’s ruling that the Tatmadaw’s attacks amounted to genocide rested on its interpretation of the crime of genocide in the ",["1948 U.N. Genocide Convention","https://ihl-databases.icrc.org/en/ihl-treaties/genocide-conv-1948"],", the first major international treaty approved by the United Nations General Assembly."]},{"k":"p","s":["For an attack to be genocidal, it must be directed against an ethnic, religious, racial or national group, and must include at least one of five prohibited acts: killing members of a group; inflicting serious physical or mental harm on members; deliberately inflicting conditions calculated to bring about its destruction; imposing measures intended to prevent births; or forcibly transferring children from the group."]},{"k":"p","s":["Beyond these factual requirements, genocide requires that the perpetrator specifically intended these acts to destroy the group, in whole or in part."]},{"k":"p","s":["In its ruling, the court agreed that the facts of Myanmar’s attacks met the legal definition of genocide. For the notoriously difficult and demanding requirement for proving the “ ",["special intent","https://www.un.org/en/genocide-prevention/definition"],"” to destroy a group, the court determined that the pattern, selective targeting and lethality of the attacks on Rohingya villages could not plausibly be explained as a counterinsurgency operation."]},{"k":"p","s":["Instead, the only reasonable inference that could be drawn from the military’s actions, the court determined, was the specific intent to destroy the Rohingya ethnic minority."]},{"k":"h","s":["A series of historic firsts"]},{"k":"p","s":["The court’s decision is unprecedented in many important respects."]},{"k":"p","s":["In an influential ",["previous ruling","https://www.icj-cij.org/case/91/judgments"]," on violations of the Genocide Convention, in Bosnia and Herzegovina v. Serbia and Montenegro in 2007, the court found only that Serbia had not met its legal duty to prevent genocide by failing to use its influence to restrain the Bosnian Serb army in the ",["Srebrenica massacre of 1995","https://www.un.org/en/observances/srebrenica-genocide-commemoration-day/about"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["In the Myanmar ruling, by contrast, the court ruled for the first time that a country is legally responsible for committing genocide – not merely failing to prevent it."]},{"k":"p","s":["Further, the court ruled for the first time that a country that has committed genocide also has multiple obligations toward the victim group. Those include designing and implementing a comprehensive program of reparations and compensation for victims; creating conditions where Rohingya can make a safe, voluntary and dignified return to their homes; and restoration of their citizenship status after national legislation from 1982 ",["rendered them stateless","https://www.migrationpolicy.org/journal/feature/stateless-and-persecuted-what-next-rohingya"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Finally, the court also demanded that Myanmar take steps to investigate all those involved in the genocide to determine individual criminal responsibility. Since the International Court of Justice is not a criminal court and only hears cases between states, this order explicitly connects the ruling to other courts where individual perpetrators can be held accountable."]},{"k":"p","s":["These include the International Criminal Court – which had ",["already requested an arrest warrant","https://news.un.org/en/story/2024/11/1157536"]," for Tatmadaw leader Min Aung Hlaing – as well as national courts that may pursue prosecution according to the doctrine of universal jurisdiction."]},{"k":"h","s":["The ruling’s broader implications"]},{"k":"p","s":["The court’s ruling in Gambia vs. Myanmar is also likely to have huge ramifications far beyond the case itself."]},{"k":"p","s":["In filing its complaint, Gambia appealed to an innovative argument to establish that it had legal standing. It argued for what’s known as “ ",["erga omnes partes","https://www.law.georgetown.edu/international-law-journal/wp-content/uploads/sites/21/2021/06/GT-GJIL210018.pdf"],",” roughly translated as “toward all parties to a treaty.” According to this line of reasoning, the Genocide Convention imposes such strong legal duties to prevent and punish the crime of genocide that any state, even one that has not in any way been directly harmed, has the standing – in fact, the obligation – to seek legal remedies."]},{"k":"p","s":["In accepting Gambia’s “erga omnes partes” approach, the court opened a pathway for other cases centering on violations of the Genocide Convention. Of these, the most significant by far is the ongoing case of ",["South Africa v. Israel","https://www.icj-cij.org/case/192"],", which charges the Israeli government and the Israeli military of committing genocide against Palestinian civilians in the Gaza Strip. Going forward, other nations would now also have a legal tool for holding perpetrator states accountable for committing the most serious international crimes."]},{"k":"p","s":["The International Court of Justice has no enforcement arm. As such, the Myanmar government cannot be compelled to abide by its rulings, whether to cease any further attacks or persecution on the Rohingya, make efforts to repatriate them or design a comprehensive reparation and compensation plan."]},{"k":"p","s":["But even if Myanmar chooses to ignore the court’s specific orders, the ruling is a major defeat. The reputational damage of being the first country found guilty of state-sponsored genocide is likely to be considerable. Further, the ruling will ",["support claims","https://specialadvisorycouncil.org/2026/09/navigating-the-forthcoming-icj-judgment-in-the-gambia-v-myanmar-a-roadmap-for-member-states/"]," that other nations have a duty not to assist Myanmar in any way that might support or enable further attacks on Rohingya."]},{"k":"p","s":["While that doesn’t automatically mean other countries will fulfill their duties under international law, many are nonetheless likely to use the ruling to bolster multilateral efforts to impose political, economic and social costs on the Tatmadaw. That could include targeted economic sanctions, financial restrictions, prohibitions on arms sales and other forms of cooperation with Myanmar’s government. The ruling thus comes with a potentially hefty price tag for the military junta."]},{"k":"p","s":["Given the general ",["weakening of international legal institutions","https://www.theguardian.com/law/2025/jun/26/are-we-witnessing-the-death-of-international-law"]," over the past 20 years, a ",["dysfunctional U.N. Security Council","https://www.economist.com/by-invitation/2025/06/24/the-uns-dysfunction-undermines-global-security-argue-ban-ki-moon-and-helen-clark"]," and an ",["International Criminal Court under siege by the Trump administration","https://theintercept.com/2026/11/17/trump-icc-sanctions-war-crimes/"],", the court’s ruling is a rare victory for international justice and opens new routes for international genocide prevention and accountability efforts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before all else, though, it is also a victory for the Rohingya – a people who have suffered decades of persecution."]},{"k":"p","s":["Thousands gathered in their Bangladeshi refugee camps to watch and cheer as the court’s president, Judge Iwasawa Yuji, read the court’s judgment. Camp inhabitants held aloft signs and ",["chanted a simple message","https://www.nytimes.com/live/2026/11/19/world/myanmar-icj-ruling-genocide"]," as the verdict came down: “Thank you Gambia.”"]}],"chars":7740}};
